7592186120026 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1045 "The Cube Root of a Perfect Cube" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186120934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120026 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "18514bce-156b-56a7-b919-0aa8cd6b4e23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120249 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120249 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33449" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120249 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120249 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\sqrt[3]{-8}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120249 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "25f6e109-0321-5e8a-b2f3-327944e47699" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120249 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that the number $-8$ is a perfect cube.\n\nSo, to determine the value of $\\sqrt[3]{-8},$ we express $-8$ as a perfect cube:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{-8} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-2)\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-2)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-2)^{3}} & = \\\\ -2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120934 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120934 #edb/ref 1061 554687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120934 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bc943f83-ca68-59a5-8d04-1f3be7f4da3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120934 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120935 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120935 #edb/ref 1061 554688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120935 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "41a11614-97fd-50d6-ae34-9ed01ba0df21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120935 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120936 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120936 #edb/ref 1061 554692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120936 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1893b834-1078-578f-b788-398a16705469" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120936 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120937 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120937 #edb/ref 1061 554696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120937 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8b332403-62f5-5fe0-ac76-52a66e2c10b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120937 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120938 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120938 #edb/ref 1061 554697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120938 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b172821f-393c-54f4-bec3-98560d9d0245" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120938 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120939 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120939 #edb/ref 1061 554701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120939 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b06bda82-f4c5-5f02-bffa-cfb125aada53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120939 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120940 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120940 #edb/ref 1061 554702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120940 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2768c295-f0d4-5823-a374-5050e8220981" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120940 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120941 #edb/ref 1061 554705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120941 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f9786bea-a98c-554e-ac43-50ebe1956098" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120941 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121142 #edb/ref 1064 "Finding the **cube root** of a number is the reverse of cubing a number. We express the cube root using the **radical symbol** $\\sqrt[3]{\\phantom{x}}.$\n\nFor example, the \"cube root of $8$\" equals $\\color{blue}2$ since \n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}2}^3 = {\\color{blue}2}\\cdot {\\color{blue}2}\\cdot {\\color{blue}2} = 8.\n$$\n\nSo, we write $\\sqrt[3]{8}={\\color{blue}2}.$\n\nSome basic cube roots are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{0} & = & \\sqrt[3]{{0}^{3}} & = & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{1} & = & \\sqrt[3]{{1}^{3}} & = & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{8} & = & \\sqrt[3]{{2}^{3}} & = & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{27} & = & \\sqrt[3]{{3}^{3}} & = & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{64} & = & \\sqrt[3]{{4}^{3}} & = & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{125} & = & \\sqrt[3]{{5}^{3}} & = & 5 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{1\\,000} & = & \\sqrt[3]{{10}^{3}} & = & 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA **perfect cube** is a number whose cube root is a whole number. So, the numbers \n\n$$\n0,\\qquad 1,\\qquad  8,\\qquad  27,\\qquad  64,\\qquad 125, \\qquad 1\\,000\n$$\n\n are all perfect cubes. You need to remember them." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121142 #edb/ref 1065 8377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121142 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "82bf149b-fb3b-506e-9c7b-3d6716081eaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121142 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121143 #edb/ref 1064 "Unlike the square root, it *is* possible to find the cube root of a negative number.\n\nFor example, $\\sqrt[3]{-8}={\\color{blue}{-2}}$ because\n\n$$\n-8 = ({\\color{blue}{-2}})^3 = ({\\color{blue}{-2}})\\cdot ({\\color{blue}{-2}})\\cdot ({\\color{blue}{-2}}).\n$$\n\nSome basic cube roots of negative numbers are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{-1} & = & \\sqrt[3]{(-1)^{3}} & = & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{-8} & = & \\sqrt[3]{(-2)^{3}} & = & -2 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{-27} & = & \\sqrt[3]{(-3)^{3}} & = & -3 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{-64} & = & \\sqrt[3]{(-4)^{3}} & = & -4 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{-125} & = & \\sqrt[3]{(-5)^{3}} & = & -5 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{-1\\,000} & = & \\sqrt[3]{(-10)^{3}} & = & -10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the numbers \n\n$$\n-1,\\qquad  -8,\\qquad  -27,\\qquad  -64,\\qquad -125, \\qquad -1\\,000\n$$\n\nare all perfect cubes." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121143 #edb/ref 1065 8378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121143 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "02c87b9c-9741-553f-a98b-da7832928f6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121143 #edb/ref 1067 "The Cube Root of a Negative Perfect Cube" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121144 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's calculate $(\\sqrt[3]{64})^3$ by performing each operation one step at a time:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\color{blue}64}\\right)^3 = \\left(\\sqrt[3]{{\\color{red}4}^3}\\right)^3 = {\\color{red}4}^3 = {\\color{blue}64}\n$$\n\nNotice that cubing the cube root gives the number under the cube root:\n\n$$\n\\left( \\sqrt[3]{64} \\right)^3 = 64\n$$\n\nThis result holds in general. If $\\color{blue}\\square$ is any number, then\n\n$$\n\\left(\\sqrt[3]{\\color{blue}\\square}\\right)^3 = {\\color{blue}\\square}.\n$$\n\nThe cube and the cube root cancel each other out, and we're left with the number that we started with.\n\n![](images/78/784f43f7253e1ed6fa394462a172e22571af06a5318b424ba2eab2157333c6fe.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121144 #edb/ref 1065 8379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121144 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "900df988-f097-53fe-8a55-39641f798d4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121144 #edb/ref 1067 "Cubing a Cube Root" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121145 #edb/ref 1064 "We can think of the cube root geometrically. For instance, let's represent the number $8$ by a collection of eight items:\n\n![](images/36/3677ea5b5f875e12fdcc6376f6b29b43a663495d20a3fbf69b4937cc61661d79.png)\n\nNow, we can pile them up in the form of a cube where each side is equal to $\\sqrt[3]{8}={\\color{blue}2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/30/305e02bdaa4c3efcb9d8047eeb3d3573f39c08714e30ba6053cfc4441053156b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121145 #edb/ref 1065 8380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121145 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "859f5c79-ff9d-5b6d-91b3-305863a271c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121145 #edb/ref 1067 "A Geometric Approach to the Cube Root" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493383 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186493995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493383 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186494013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493383 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186494056 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493383 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493383 #edb/ref 1045 "The Cube Root of a Perfect Cube" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493383 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186493995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493383 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493383 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493383 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "9b8dddd1-da8a-515b-b440-7da08015b94d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493421 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493421 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493421 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11db075b-d65e-51e5-8dca-f8e9ab1adb79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493467 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493467 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493467 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2cbd15cf-50e0-5f6c-a023-66b7777a5ea1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493533 #edb/ref 1080 "-1,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493533 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493533 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5c730b9a-1755-532b-b8d1-24d3aece98b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493544 #edb/ref 1080 "100" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493544 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592